/// ### What it does
/// Checks for impls of `From<..>` that contain `panic!()` or `unwrap()`
///
/// ### Why is this bad?
/// `TryFrom` should be used if there's a possibility of failure.
///
/// ### Example
/// ```no_run
/// struct Foo(i32);
///
/// impl From<String> for Foo {
///     fn from(s: String) -> Self {
///         Foo(s.parse().unwrap())
///     }
/// }
/// ```
///
/// Use instead:
